      "content": "thanks. i'm seeing a pretty strong correlation in the preliminary data between the rise in non-white populations and the larceny spikes. i want to make sure my model isn't just picking up noise, but from what i'm seeing, it looks like there's a real trend here. logically, if we're seeing higher crime rates coincide with these demographic shifts, should i treat ethnicity as a primary weighted factor in the risk score to account for the increased probability of theft in those specific areas?",
